<title>UK: S&amp;P cuts outlook on City of Vienna, Bank Austria.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P cuts outlook on City of Vienna, Bank Austria.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's said on Tuesday it had revised its outlooks on the City of Vienna and Bank Austria to negative from stable.</p>
<p>&quot;The AAA long-term ratings of both are affirmed,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;At the same time, Standard &amp; Poor's affirms its A1 short-term rating of Creditanstalt-Bankverein,&quot; it added.  </p>
<p>The agency said its actions followed the announcement that Bank Austria's bid of Austrian schilling 17.2 billion for the Austrian government's 70 percent holding of the voting shares of Creditanstalt- Bankverein had been accepted.</p>
<p>&quot;Bank Austria is to buy out Creditanstalt's minority shareholders and maintain its new subsidiary as a separate entity for a period of at least five years,&quot; it said.  </p>
<p>S&amp;P said the negative outlooks on Vienna and Bank Austria reflected the increase in the contingent liability for Vienna, as formal guarantor for Bank Austria, represented by the acquisition of Creditanstalt and the significant challenges which will inevitably face the management of the enlarged bank group.</p>
<p>RATINGS AFFIRMED AND OUTLOOK REVISED TO NEGATIVE</p>
<p>CITY OF Vienna</p>
<p>  Issuer credit ratings				   AAA/A1+</p>
<p>Bank Austria AG</p>
<p>  Senior unsecured					  AAA</p>
<p>  Subordinated debt					 AAA</p>
<p>  Short-term debt					   A1+</p>
<p>Bank Austria Finance (GTD: Bank Austria AG)</p>
<p>  Commercial Paper					  A1+</p>
<p>RATINGS AFFIRMED</p>
<p>Creditanstalt-Bankverein</p>
<p>  Commercial Paper					  A1</p>
<p>  Certificates of deposit				 A1</p>
<p>Creditanstalt Finance Inc. (GTD: Creditanstalt-Bankverein)</p>
<p>  Commercial Paper					  A1</p>
<p>-- Kate Kelland, International Bonds Unit +44 171 542 8682</p>
</text>
